# SDLC (opt-in)

Invoke manually (`@sdlc`) or when unsure which workflow to use. **Do not treat this as always-on process.**

## Pick a path

| Situation | What to run |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Build / implement / fix end-to-end** | **`ship-feature` skill** — full wave loop (grill → research → slice → test → code → validate∥guard → comment∥review → commit → memory) |
| Quick fix, 1–2 files, clear scope | Graph scout (see `main.mdc`) → implement. Skip ship-feature. |
| Touching a **god node** | Graph scout + drill **before** editing |
| Need a written spec doc | gstack `/spec` *(optional — `INSTALL_GSTACK=1 bash setup`)* |
| Browser / deploy QA | gstack `/qa`, `/ship` *(optional)* |

---

## ship-feature (primary)

Use when the user says *build this*, *implement X*, *add feature*, *fix and ship*, or any end-to-end request.

**Rules:**
- **Wave 0 (grill) finishes before any sub-agent** — one question at a time, with your recommended answer.
- **Wave 1.5 (slice fan-out)** — parent splits Research into independent change slices before Wave 2.
- **Test before code, isolated** — Test agent gets per-slice `<TEST SPEC>` only; Code agent gets per-slice `<CODE BRIEF>` only. Neither sees the other's output.
- **Parent applies test files** after Wave 2 before launching Wave 3 Code for that slice.
- **One sub-agent per Task** — parallel agents only within the same wave, in a single message; independent slices may parallelize at the same wave.
- **Wave 5.5 (commit slice)** — one `git commit` per slice after validate/review green; `post-commit.sh` runs graphify + memory compress. No PR step.
- **Wave 6 memory** — parent writes session notes; each slice commit already rolled `memory/state.yaml`.

Full wave prompts → `.agents/skills/ship-feature/SKILL.md`

---

## memory-graph integration

| After work | Where it goes |
|------------|---------------|
| Open threads, one-line state | `context:` / `open:` in today's `sessions/*.md` |
| Rolled-up working memory | `memory/state.yaml` *(auto, every file-changing stop)* |
| God nodes touched | Session frontmatter + graph scout summary |
| Pattern or convention changed | Relevant `.agents/skills/` file + `AGENTS.md` index *(same change)* |

No hook followup for session capture. No prose *Decisions* essays — git diff is *what*; memory is *what's still open*.

**Before starting a feature:** read `memory/state.yaml` + scan `memory.md`.
**Before editing hooks/tests:** load `memory-graph-conventions` skill.

---

## Graph

Never load `graphify-out/graph.json` into parent chat. Scout subagent → optional drill if HIGH/CRITICAL. See `main.mdc` and `graph-scout` skill.

